**/target/
*.class
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# Web
amarillo-web/node_modules/
amarillo-web/dist/

# Claude Code agent worktrees (ephemeral, per-agent)
.claude/worktrees/

# Personal per-user Claude Code project settings (local overrides)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Saved fleets are player data, not source. Tests that need one build it and
# delete it again (FleetStorageEndpointTest), so nothing here is a fixture.
data/fleets/

# Saved games are player data, not source — the same reasoning as data/fleets above.
# SaveGameEndpointTest writes here and deletes what it wrote; anything left behind is
# a leftover, never a fixture. The server resolves this relative to its working
# directory, so a test run from amarillo-server/ creates amarillo-server/data/saves.
data/saves/
amarillo-server/data/

# Rulebook PDFs. Kept on disk so they can be consulted while working, never
# committed: they are ADB's copyrighted product, watermarked with the buyer's
# name and order number, and this repo has a public remote.
data/rules/

# ...and a rulebook dropped anywhere else. The directory rule above only guards one
# folder, and the thing we must never publish is the FILE, wherever it lands. The repo
# tracks no PDFs at all, so this un-tracks nothing. If you ever do want one in the repo,
# `git add -f <file>` still works.
*.pdf
